= Automaton — Simple =

A computational '''automaton''' is a simplified mathematical machine.

It has states and rules that tell it how to move from one state to another.

Some automata read a string one symbol at a time and decide whether the string belongs to a formal language.

Different automata have different abilities.

A finite automaton has only finite memory in its state.

A pushdown automaton adds a stack.

A [[Turing machine/Simple|Turing machine]] has a much more powerful idealized memory model.

